0:{"rsc":["$","$1","c",{"children":[["$","$L2",null,{"study":{"id":"privacy","title":"Privacy is not an optional extra","category":"Landmark judgment","year":"2017","subtitle":"K.S. Puttaswamy v. Union of India","fictional":false,"difficulty":"Law & rights","summary":"A nine-judge bench recognized privacy as a fundamental right, shaping how digital investigative powers must be understood.","story":["The case arose in a context that included challenges to the Aadhaar framework and broader questions about informational privacy. A nine-judge bench examined whether the Constitution protected privacy.","The Court recognized privacy as a fundamental right and discussed its relationship with life, liberty, autonomy, dignity, and other freedoms. The judgment did not make every restriction unconstitutional; it required a proper legal and constitutional basis.","For investigators, the practical lesson is to connect each collection action to authority, legitimate purpose, proportionality, and safeguards. A device contains far more than the relevant message. Scope, minimization, secure handling, and accountable access are not optional additions to a technically successful acquisition."],"timeline":[{"date":"2017","event":"Nine-judge bench recognizes the fundamental right to privacy."},{"date":"2018 onward","event":"Related proceedings address the Aadhaar framework."},{"date":"2023","event":"The DPDP Act creates a separate statutory personal-data framework."}],"issue":"Constitutional protection of privacy and the framework for evaluating state interference.","holding":"Privacy is a fundamental right. The legality and justification of a particular restriction require analysis of the applicable right, measure, and safeguards.","lessons":["Authority comes before technical convenience.","Collect within a defined and relevant scope.","Protect unrelated personal information.","Record the purpose and proportionality of material decisions.","Distinguish constitutional principles from a specific statute’s operational rules."],"questions":["How would you narrow a cloud-record request?","What should a device examination plan say about unrelated data?","Why does public availability not settle every privacy question?"],"sources":["privacy","constitution","dpdp"],"topics":["1.3","2.3","2.12"]}}],[["$","script","script-0",{"src":"/_next/static/chunks/07qngb6s2_y2q.js","async":true}]],["$","$L3",null,{"children":["$","$4",null,{"name":"Next.MetadataOutlet","children":"$@5"}]}]]}],"isPartial":false,"staleTime":300,"varyParams":null,"buildId":"mMiCr23A_-Cpk0hZkfT7X"}
